Local patch for poingstudios/godot-admob-plugin v5.1.0 (game-template).

Removes the plugin's automatic binary download:
- admob.gd: BinaryInstaller.install_missing_binaries_sync() would run
  `which curl` + `curl -L -o ...` via OS.execute in headless mode when
  addons/admob/{android,ios}/bin/package.gd is missing.
- editor_menu.gd: check_dependencies() would auto-download the same files
  with HTTPRequest when the GUI editor starts.
The binaries are committed instead (see docs/plugin-review.md).

Re-apply after every plugin update:  git apply patches/admob-no-autodownload.patch
Check it is applied:                  make plugin-check

--- a/addons/admob/admob.gd	2026-10-24 19:47:35.113198126 +0200
+++ b/addons/admob/admob.gd	2026-10-24 19:47:35.125536277 +0200
@@ -38,7 +38,8 @@
 
 func _enter_tree() -> void:
 	CSharpService.manage_visibility(self)
-	BinaryInstaller.install_missing_binaries_sync()
+	# LOCAL PATCH (patches/admob-no-autodownload.patch): never download or shell out.
+	# BinaryInstaller.install_missing_binaries_sync()
 	ProjectSettingsService.register_settings()
 
 	add_export_plugin(_main_exporter)
--- a/addons/admob/internal/editor/editor_menu.gd	2026-10-24 19:47:35.118161994 +0200
+++ b/addons/admob/internal/editor/editor_menu.gd	2026-10-24 19:47:35.127141494 +0200
@@ -58,9 +58,10 @@
 	_android_handler = AndroidHandler.new(DownloadService.new(host), _dialog_service)
 	_ios_handler = IOSHandler.new(DownloadService.new(host), _dialog_service)
 
-	if DisplayServer.get_name() != "headless":
-		_android_handler.check_dependencies()
-		_ios_handler.check_dependencies()
+	# LOCAL PATCH (patches/admob-no-autodownload.patch): no automatic download on editor start.
+	# if DisplayServer.get_name() != "headless":
+	# 	_android_handler.check_dependencies()
+	# 	_ios_handler.check_dependencies()
 
 	_setup_menu()
 
